cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. All results are model predictions, conditional on qualitative outcomes reported in the literature; nothing is validated on the author's own devices."
title: "Bayesian optimization of VCSEL oxide-aperture geometry for polarization-switching photonic Ising machines (literature-anchored simulation study)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Morozova
    given-names: Polina
version: 0.6.0
date-released: 2026-10-10
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hakainasan/vcsel-polarization-bo"
abstract: >
  Spin-flip-model yield simulator, geometry-to-anisotropy layer, literature-anchored approximate Bayesian computation over the
  unknown wafer constants, Gaussian-process Bayesian optimisation with baselines, and portfolio design of a fabrication batch
  for oxide-aperture shapes of polarization-switchable VCSELs. Results are simulated with a reduced, uncalibrated model that is
  constrained only by qualitative outcomes of published experiments and require experimental validation. Includes the design
  of mask 2, an aperture-elongation ruler for calibrating a wafer's native anisotropy.
keywords: [VCSEL, polarization switching, machine learning, Gaussian process regression, Bayesian optimization, spin-flip model, photonic Ising machine, approximate Bayesian computation, photomask design]
